It is possible, but they must be set up in the same variable.

For example, x[t, 1:nStates] can be a vector of the states at time t, and x[t+1, 1:nStates] depends on x[t, 1:nStates] however you need.  You can still declare x[t, 1], x[t, 2], etc. separately, so it should be simply a matter of how latent states are named and organized.

