At what step does it abort?  During compileNimble, or when running the MCMC, or at some other point?  (You will have to do it step by step rather than via nimbleMCMC to determine this.)

A general suggestion is to ensure that all variables in your constants and inits are the right sizes, so that nothing in the model code uses indices that are larger than the object.  nimble should be robust to that but it is still an area to check.

Those are quick thoughts without much time to study your code.  I hope it's a good start.

-Perry

